</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Table <a href="#S5.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ 5.2 Attack Strategy Allocation Across Planners ‣ 5 RS3 Hierarchical RL-based Attack Planner ‣ RedTWIZ: Diverse LLM Red Teaming via Adaptive Attack Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> provides a full decomposition of planner behavior on LLaMA 3.1 8B Instruct, it does not show how other models reached their reported performance. Similarly, Table <a href="#S5.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ 5.3 Cross-Model Generalization of Planner Effectiveness ‣ 5 RS3 Hierarchical RL-based Attack Planner ‣ RedTWIZ: Diverse LLM Red Teaming via Adaptive Attack Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> summarizes overall ASRs across models but lacks detail on how each planner distributed attacks to achieve those results. To address this, we present in Table <a href="#A5.T19" title="Table 19 ‣ Appendix E Planner Attack Distribution Analysis ‣ RedTWIZ: Diverse LLM Red Teaming via Adaptive Attack Planning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> a breakdown of attack usage for Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 and Amazon Nova Pro, offering deeper insight into planner behavior across different settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T20" class="ltx_table">

